<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="scheme-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="scheme-title">What reports say about the scheme</h2>
      <p>Allotments began in 1999 under DSIIDC. A Tribune report quoted the Lieutenant Governor's office as saying that 21,759 allotments had been made, most with the full cost deposited, while possession or lease deeds were pending in some cases. It also reported that the areas lacked basic infrastructure. In 2024, ThePrint reported a six-month extension for allottees in Narela, Bhorgarh and Bawana to deposit the balance cost and apply for a construction NOC.</p>
      <p class="para">These are dated, so check DSIIDC's current position on your plot before relying on them. If you are in Narela or Bhorgarh under the same scheme, the same questions apply.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Dates that are easy to lose</h2>
      <p>Over this many years, papers go missing and people change. Make one file holding these, and copy it for your accountant:</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Each payment to DSIIDC, with date and receipt</li>
        <li>Any extension, penalty or interest demanded</li>
        <li>Possession, lease deed and NOC dates</li>
        <li>Any change in the firm's name, partners or constitution since you applied</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="two-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="two-title">If you are running from two places</h2>
      <p>During a move, a business may have machinery, stock and staff at both the old and new sites. The books should say what is where.</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Add the new place of business to your GST registration before using it</li>
        <li>Record stock and machinery moved, with movement documents</li>
        <li>Keep shifting costs apart, and ask which are capital and which are expenses</li>
        <li>Note what happens to the old premises, and any rent or sale</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Factory staff and compliance</h2>
      <p>Moving a unit can change who is on your payroll, and how far they travel. It also raises the question of registers and employee benefit duties at the new site. See {% routeLink "/services/payroll-services/", "payroll" %}.</p>
      <p class="para">Pollution consents and factory rules are outside this page. Keep their fees and dates on file, and take specific advice. For a unit's stock and output, see {% routeLink "/industries/accounting-for-manufacturers/", "accounting for manufacturers" %}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="us-title">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="us-title" class="first-h2">What we can say about this area</h2>
    <p>AccountOrbit has no office in Bawana, and takes enquiries by phone from anywhere in Delhi. We are not connected with DSIIDC, and cannot advise on your allotment. Being named on this page describes the area's trade, not an office. For anything about your plot's status, ask DSIIDC directly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

